WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:05.030 line:80%
A computer-vision model
on its own is not a product: annotation,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.240 line:80%
training and live execution have to agree.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.870 line:80%
One control plane keeps
projects, data sets,

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.970 line:80%
jobs and models
in a single application state,

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.790 line:80%
and the services work
through its contracts.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.570 line:80%
Training workers claim jobs
from the queue and send heartbeats;

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.680 line:80%
progress and results return
to the control plane.

00:00:29.865 --> 00:00:31.725 line:80%
Models ship as plugins,

00:00:31.735 --> 00:00:35.825 line:80%
and annotation and training load them
through shared interfaces,

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.605 line:80%
so the services stay separate.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.960 line:80%
Live cameras feed a media relay, and each
visual workflow runs in its own worker,

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.280 line:80%
with retries for failing nodes.

00:00:48.605 --> 00:00:53.915 line:80%
The product appears here through its
documented architecture: no client data,

00:00:53.925 --> 00:00:57.485 line:80%
no internal hostnames
and no private interface.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:03.845 line:80%
The result is a connected model life cycle
with clear boundaries between data,

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:05.515 line:80%
models and execution.
